      "seed": 1518545724,
      "version": 1473,
      "versionNonce": 1250536683,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790053488148,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. child class of Map .\n\n2. stores data in key value pair . Key must be unique .\n\n3. It stores the data as Entry object . Entry is an inner\ninterface store inside Map .\n\n\n\nMethods of Map\n===============\n\n1. put (Object key, Object value ) : takes two parameter\nkey and value .\n\nIf key is not present in Map, then it creates a new Object\nof Entry type and initializes it with key and value , then\nadd it in Map and returns null .\n\nIf key is found in Map then it replaces the old value with\nnew value and returns old value .\n\n2. get () (Object key ) : It takes key as arguement\nsearches in  Map, if key is present in Map it returns it's\nvalue otherwise returns null .\n\n3. size ( ) : Returns total number of key value pair stored\nin Map .\n\n4. clear( ) : remove all the key value pair from the Map .\n\n5. containsKey ( Object key ) : If key is present in Map\nreturns true , otherwise returns false .\n\n6. containsValue ( Object value) : If value a is present in\nMap returns true , otherwise returns false .\n\n7. remove ( Object key ) : It searhes the key in the Map .\n\nIf found delete it's entry and returns its value , otherwise\nreturns null .\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. child class of Map .\n\n2. stores data in key value pair . Key must be unique .\n\n3. It stores the data as Entry object . Entry is an inner interface store inside Map .\n\n\n\nMethods of Map\n===============\n\n1. put (Object key, Object value ) : takes two parameter key and value .\n\nIf key is not present in Map, then it creates a new Object of Entry type and initializes it with key and value , then add it in Map and returns null .\n\nIf key is found in Map then it replaces the old value with new value and returns old value .\n\n2. get () (Object key ) : It takes key as arguement searches in  Map, if key is present in Map it returns it's value otherwise returns null .\n\n3. size ( ) : Returns total number of key value pair stored in Map .\n\n4. clear( ) : remove all the key value pair from the Map .\n\n5. containsKey ( Object key ) : If key is present in Map returns true , otherwise returns false .\n\n6. containsValue ( Object value) : If value a is present in Map returns true , otherwise returns false .\n\n7. remove ( Object key ) : It searhes the key in the Map .\n\nIf found delete it's entry and returns its value , otherwise returns null .\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
